* APOLLO 11 AS FLOWN: A VIEW-1108 SCENARIO (A RUN DECK, IN 1969 TERMS).
*
* A scenario is one mission's data as one source tells it: this one is the
* mission as flown, from the post-flight reports.  A pre-flight nominal
* scenario for the same mission would be a second file with its own ID.
* One card per line.  A card starting with * is a comment.  Fields are
* KEY=VALUE; times are g.e.t. h:mm:ss.s from this mission's range zero.
* tools/gen_data.py turns every data/scenarios/*.scn into BLOCK DATA
* (src/viewdata.f).
* SRC is carried into viewdata.f as a comment next to the card's data.
*
* Sources:
*   MR  Apollo 11 Mission Report, MSC-00171, November 1969.  NASA re-scan
*       https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/static/apollo50th/pdf/A11_MissionReport.pdf
*       (printed page numbers).  Table 7-II, p. 7-9, gives latitudes as
*       geodetic for the Earth and selenographic for the Moon (Table 7-I,
*       p. 7-8); altitudes in n mi; flight-path angle and heading space-fixed.
*   SP  R. W. Orloff, Apollo by the Numbers, NASA SP-2000-4029 (printed pages).
*
* Card types:
*   SCENARIO ID= (1, 2, ... across all files)  MISSION=  NAME=
*   EPOCH    JD=  (range zero, Julian date)
*   SITE     LAT= LON= AZ=  (lunar landing site, deg, and descent azimuth)
*   LEG      TYPE=CIRC|CONIC|LUNAR  FROM= TO=  (g.e.t. span it covers)
*     CIRC   Earth circular orbit through a state: T= LAT= LON= HDG=, orbit
*            altitude ALT= (n mi).  LATTYPE=GC geocentric, GD geodetic.
*     CONIC  Earth-centred conic from a state: T= LAT= LON= ALT= V= (ft/s)
*            FPA= HDG= (deg).
*     LUNAR  Moon circular orbit through two states, T= LAT= LON= and
*            TB= LATB= LONB= (selenographic), N= whole revolutions between
*            them, ALT= (n mi).  The plane and the mean motion come from
*            the two states.
*   EVENT    KIND= T=
*
SCENARIO ID=1 MISSION="APOLLO 11" NAME="AS FLOWN"
EPOCH JD=2440419.063889 SRC="MR Table 3-I p. 3-4: range zero 13:32:00 G.m.t., July 16, 1969"
SITE LAT=0.67416 LON=23.47314 AZ=268.8 SRC="NSSDC Apollo Landing Site Coordinates, citing Wagner et al., Icarus 283 (2017), mean Earth/polar axis; MR p. 3-2 gives 0 41 15 N, 23 26 E on ORB-II-6 (1967). Azimuth 268.8: ours, near the 269.0 fitted to MR Table 7-II"
*
* Earth parking orbit.  The S-IVB first cutoff state, geocentric latitude,
* on a circle at the mean of the MR's 100.7 by 99.2 n mi (p. 3-1).
LEG TYPE=CIRC FROM=0:11:49.33 TO=2:44:16.2 T=0:11:39.33 LATTYPE=GC LAT=32.4865 LON=-53.4588 V=25561.6 FPA=0.011 HDG=88.414 ALT=99.95 SRC="SP p. 103 ascent table, S-IVB 1st burn cutoff: geocentric 32.4865 N, -53.4588 E, space-fixed velocity 25,561.6, flight-path angle 0.011, heading 88.414; orbit MR p. 3-1"
*
* Translunar coast: two conics, from translunar injection and from the
* first midcourse correction cutoff.  Earth only (no lunar gravity): ours.
LEG TYPE=CONIC FROM=2:50:13.2 TO=26:44:58.7 T=2:50:13.2 LATTYPE=GD LAT=9.98 LON=-164.84 ALT=180.6 V=35546 FPA=7.37 HDG=60.07 SRC="MR Table 7-II p. 7-9, translunar injection"
LEG TYPE=CONIC FROM=26:44:58.7 TO=75:49:50.4 T=26:45:01.8 LATTYPE=GD LAT=6.00 LON=-11.17 ALT=109477.2 V=5010.0 FPA=76.88 HDG=120.87 SRC="MR Table 7-II p. 7-9, first midcourse correction cutoff"
*
* Lunar orbit: after insertion (an ellipse, 169.7 by 60.0 n mi, SP p. 104,
* put on a circle through its two rows at their mean altitude: ours), after
* circularization, and after undocking.  Rows from MR Table 7-II; the
* revolution counts are ours, from the periods those rows imply (7113 s
* after circularization).
LEG TYPE=LUNAR FROM=75:49:50.4 TO=80:11:36.8 T=75:55:48.0 LAT=0.16 LON=167.13 TB=80:11:36.8 LATB=-0.02 LONB=170.09 N=1 ALT=114.9 SRC="MR Table 7-II p. 7-9, lunar orbit insertion cutoff and circularization ignition; altitude the mean of SP p. 104's 169.7 by 60.0 n mi"
LEG TYPE=LUNAR FROM=80:11:36.8 TO=100:12:00.0 T=80:11:53.5 LAT=-0.02 LON=169.16 TB=100:12:00.0 LATB=1.11 LONB=116.21 N=10 ALT=62.2 SRC="MR Table 7-II p. 7-9, circularization cutoff and undocking; altitude the mean of the two rows"
LEG TYPE=LUNAR FROM=100:12:00.0 TO=135:23:42.3 T=100:40:01.9 LAT=1.05 LON=31.41 TB=130:09:31.2 LATB=1.10 LONB=41.85 N=14 ALT=62.0 SRC="MR Table 7-II p. 7-9, separation cutoff and ascent stage jettison; altitude the mean of the two rows"
*
* Transearth coast: conics from the second midcourse correction, from
* command module/service module separation, and from entry interface.
LEG TYPE=CONIC FROM=135:26:13.7 TO=150:29:57.4 T=150:29:57.4 LATTYPE=GD LAT=-13.16 LON=-37.79 ALT=169087.2 V=4075.0 FPA=-80.34 HDG=129.30 SRC="MR Table 7-II p. 7-9, second midcourse correction ignition"
LEG TYPE=CONIC FROM=150:30:07.4 TO=195:03:05.7 T=194:49:12.7 LATTYPE=GD LAT=-35.09 LON=122.54 ALT=1778.3 V=29615.5 FPA=-35.26 HDG=69.27 SRC="MR Table 7-II p. 7-9, command module/service module separation"
LEG TYPE=CONIC FROM=195:03:05.7 TO=196:00:00 T=195:03:05.7 LATTYPE=GD LAT=-3.19 LON=171.96 ALT=65.8 V=36194.4 FPA=-6.48 HDG=50.18 SRC="MR Table 7-VII p. 7-12, entry interface (400 000 ft)"
*
* Events the kernel keys on.
EVENT KIND=TDATT T=3:09:20 SRC="Apollo 11 Flight Journal 002:54:09: S-IVB manoeuvre to separation attitude to be completed at plus 09 plus 20"
EVENT KIND=SEP T=3:17:04.6 SRC="MR Table 3-I p. 3-4 and Table 7-II p. 7-9: command module/S-IVB separation. SP p. 104 has CSM separated from S-IVB at 003:15:23.00 and 003:17:04.60 as the separation manoeuvre ignition"
EVENT KIND=APPR T=3:20:30 SRC="Our guess: start of the docking approach, between separation and Collins' I'm still quite a ways at 003:22:25 (Flight Journal)"
EVENT KIND=DOCK T=3:24:03.1 SRC="MR Table 3-I p. 3-4 and Table 7-II p. 7-9; SP p. 104 has 003:24:03.70"
EVENT KIND=UNDOCK T=100:12:00.0 SRC="MR Table 3-I p. 3-4"
EVENT KIND=TOUCH T=102:45:39.9 SRC="MR Table 3-I p. 3-4, lunar landing"
EVENT KIND=EI T=195:03:05.7 SRC="MR Table 7-VII p. 7-12, entry interface"
EVENT KIND=PTC T=10:58:19 SRC="Apollo 11 Flight Journal, 010:58:19, Collins: PTC is started now"
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* SIMULATION (src/sim.f): the START state, the SCORE (burns) and the
* REFERENCE rows the engine checks against or, with state vector updates
* on, resets to.  The period counterpart of these cards is the
* Spacecraft Operational Trajectory and its per-burn "target loads" (MSC
* IN 69-FM-96, Apollo 10, Vol. I; see docs/simulation.md); these cards
* hold the as-flown values instead.  Cards are KEY=VALUE with a SRC;
* tools/gen_data.py ignores unknown keys with a warning, so a BURN can
* later carry TRIGGER= (when it fires) and TARGET= (its cutoff condition).
*
*   START  T= and a state as a CONIC leg's (BODY=EARTH), END= the time
*          the run stops.
*   BURN   T= mid-burn g.e.t. (the ignition time plus half the firing
*          time, so one impulse stands for the burn: ours), DV= ft/s,
*          BODY= the body whose frame the direction is in, and the
*          direction P= (along the velocity) R= (in the orbit plane,
*          away from the body) N= (along the orbit normal).
*   REF    T= and a sourced state.  BODY=EARTH: as a CONIC leg's.
*          BODY=MOON: selenographic LAT= LON=, ALT=, V=, FPA=; the
*          horizontal direction is taken from the lunar leg's plane at
*          that time (MR Table 7-II's lunar headings are not in a frame
*          we can use; see the a11 profile notes).
*
* Burns left out, all below 2.5 ft/s: CSM/S-IVB separation 0.7 ft/s at
* 3:17:04.6 (MR Table 7-III p. 7-10; the CSM docked back and flew with
* the S-IVB stack until ejection), CSM/LM separation 1.4 ft/s at
* 100:39:52.9 and final separation 2.2 ft/s at 130:30:01.0 (MR Table
* 7-V p. 7-11), whose directions we have no source for.
*
START T=2:50:13.2 END=195:10:00 BODY=EARTH LATTYPE=GD LAT=9.98 LON=-164.84 ALT=180.6 V=35546 FPA=7.37 HDG=60.07 SRC="MR Table 7-II p. 7-9, translunar injection"
*
BURN T=4:40:03.25 DV=19.7 BODY=EARTH P=-0.798 R=0.600 N=0.052 SRC="MR Table 7-III p. 7-10: spacecraft/S-IVB separation, SPS, ignition 4:40:01.8, 2.9 s, 19.7 ft/s. Direction derived by us from the Table 7-II ignition and cutoff rows"
BURN T=26:45:00.25 DV=20.9 BODY=EARTH P=-0.711 R=0.703 N=-0.009 SRC="MR Table 7-III p. 7-10: first midcourse correction, SPS, ignition 26:44:58.7, 3.1 s, 20.9 ft/s. Direction derived by us from the Table 7-II ignition and cutoff rows"
BURN T=75:52:49.15 DV=2917.5 BODY=MOON P=-1 R=0 N=0 SRC="MR Table 7-V p. 7-11: lunar orbit insertion, SPS, ignition 75:49:50.4, 357.5 s, 2917.5 ft/s. Direction against the velocity: our assumption"
BURN T=80:11:45.2 DV=158.8 BODY=MOON P=-1 R=0 N=0 SRC="MR Table 7-V p. 7-11: lunar orbit circularization, SPS, ignition 80:11:36.8, 16.8 s, 158.8 ft/s. Direction against the velocity: our assumption"
BURN T=135:25:18.0 DV=3279.0 BODY=MOON P=1 R=0 N=0 SRC="MR Table 7-VI p. 7-11: transearth injection, SPS, ignition 135:23:42.3, 151.4 s, 3279.0 ft/s. Direction along the velocity: our assumption"
BURN T=150:30:03.0 DV=4.8 BODY=EARTH P=-0.198 R=0.980 N=0.000 SRC="MR Table 7-VI p. 7-11: second midcourse correction, SM RCS, ignition 150:29:57.4, 11.2 s, 4.8 ft/s. Direction derived by us from the Table 7-II ignition and cutoff rows"
*
* Reference rows: MR Table 7-II p. 7-9 (and 7-VII p. 7-12 for entry).
* Not used: the command module/S-IVB separation row (3:17:04.6) sits
* about 0.28 deg of longitude (60 km) off the conic through the TLI row,
* while the 4:40 row agrees with that conic to 0.04 deg; correcting to
* it made the 4:40 error worse (184 km against 50 km uncorrected).
* REF T=3:17:04.6 BODY=EARTH LATTYPE=GD LAT=31.16 LON=-88.76 ALT=4110.9 V=24456.8 FPA=46.24 HDG=95.10 SRC="command module/S-IVB separation"
REF T=4:40:04.7 BODY=EARTH LATTYPE=GD LAT=21.16 LON=-68.46 ALT=16627.3 V=14663.0 FPA=64.25 HDG=113.74 SRC="separation manoeuvre cutoff"
REF T=26:45:01.8 BODY=EARTH LATTYPE=GD LAT=6.00 LON=-11.17 ALT=109477.2 V=5010.0 FPA=76.88 HDG=120.87 SRC="first midcourse correction cutoff"
REF T=75:55:48.0 BODY=MOON LAT=0.16 LON=167.13 ALT=60.1 V=5479.0 FPA=-0.20 SRC="lunar orbit insertion cutoff"
REF T=80:11:53.5 BODY=MOON LAT=-0.02 LON=169.16 ALT=61.6 V=5338.3 FPA=0.32 SRC="lunar orbit circularization cutoff"
REF T=100:12:00.0 BODY=MOON LAT=1.11 LON=116.21 ALT=62.9 V=5333.8 FPA=0.16 SRC="undocking"
REF T=100:40:01.9 BODY=MOON LAT=1.05 LON=31.41 ALT=62.5 V=5332.2 FPA=-0.16 SRC="separation cutoff"
REF T=128:03:00.0 BODY=MOON LAT=1.18 LON=67.31 ALT=60.6 V=5341.5 FPA=0.16 SRC="docking"
REF T=130:09:31.2 BODY=MOON LAT=1.10 LON=41.85 ALT=61.6 V=5335.9 FPA=0.15 SRC="ascent stage jettison"
REF T=135:23:42.3 BODY=MOON LAT=-0.16 LON=164.02 ALT=52.4 V=5376.0 FPA=-0.03 SRC="transearth injection ignition"
REF T=150:30:07.4 BODY=EARTH LATTYPE=GD LAT=-13.16 LON=-37.83 ALT=169080.6 V=4074.0 FPA=-80.41 HDG=129.30 SRC="second midcourse correction cutoff"
REF T=194:49:12.7 BODY=EARTH LATTYPE=GD LAT=-35.09 LON=122.54 ALT=1778.3 V=29615.5 FPA=-35.26 HDG=69.27 SRC="command module/service module separation"
REF T=195:03:05.7 BODY=EARTH LATTYPE=GD LAT=-3.19 LON=171.96 ALT=65.8 V=36194.4 FPA=-6.48 HDG=50.18 SRC="MR Table 7-VII p. 7-12, entry interface"
